From 9d74b22a1348faed5f300424cea2e0eccdcc3abf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: purplewall1206 <purplewall1206@github.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 07:41:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mm: CortenMM arena: MODE spatial routing
 (mprotect/madvise/mremap) and counters

T0b (M4T0_SPEC.md sec 3.3-3.5/5.8/8-T0-R1): in MODE-process takeover,
route spatial operations that touch an arena into descriptor-guarded
transactions instead of blanket -EOPNOTSUPP rejects:

- mprotect: an in-arena permission change becomes a corten_mark()
  transaction under the covering desc write lock; whole-arena commits
  also move the shadow-VMA flags and the FRESH fault gate, with the
  rewritten range TLB-flushed (JVM PROT_NONE-reserve + commit shape).
- madvise: MADV_FREE folds into the DONTNEED content-drop transaction
  (counted); NORMAL/SEQUENTIAL/RANDOM/COLD become in-arena counted
  no-op successes; everything else keeps the counted reject.
- mremap: shrink returns the same address and drops the tail through
  the chunk-zap transaction; grow kernel-copies into a fresh window
  arena and RELEASEs the old one (STATE D12/OQ-A closed); MREMAP_FIXED,
  DONTUNMAP and boundary crossings stay counted rejects.
- named route counters rendered by the debugfs arena_stats report
  (auto_mmaps, mprotect_routes, mremap_routes, rearm_*, eagain_*,
  mremap_release_fail); the zero-modification DoD runner (LD_PRELOAD
  constructor hook + run_t0_dod.sh) lives project-side.

Defect-fix ledger, review/verify rounds to D-G' (anchors in
cortenmm/results/r04/t0b-verify.md):
- B2: drop the nonexistent MADV_FREE_LOCKED case from the madvise
  decision table (uapi has no locked FREE variant).
- D-E: protect_range whole leg must vm_flags_clear(R/W/X) before the
  re-set -- vm_flags_set only ORs, so a downshift left stale perms.
- D-F: dontneed_route normalizes its return (0=legacy, 1=routed) so a
  successful zap is no longer misread as "range not ours".
- D-G: chunk-mprotect on an untracked window re-arms the upper table
  and records pending per-window perms, fixing the JVM reserve+commit
  first-touch shape (KUnit anchor: mprotect_fresh).
- D-G': descriptor-missing windows (-EOPNOTSUPP/-ENOENT from the lock)
  retry one fill_upper() re-arm before the legacy self-heal, counted
  by rearm_recovered/rearm_failed (KUnit anchor: untracked_rearm).
- review C1: the route exits retry the transient PT-retirement -EAGAIN
  once and count the residual (eagain_leaked) instead of leaking
  EAGAIN past mprotect/mremap/madvise(2), where libc never retries.
- review C2: a mremap grow RELEASE failure rolls back the fresh window
  (mremap_release_fail) so the caller only sees the error and keeps
  the old block with its content intact.

Known residual, registered for later slices (repro: dg_probe2):
- D-G'': JVM CDS relocation abort (ACCERR, si_addr 0x100086000010
  shape) -- independent root cause, under investigation; full java
  boot under MODE stays out of this slice.
- fork boundary (DEV-11): arena commits do not survive fork demotion;
  OQ filed to the planner.

Verification: =y full build RC=0, zero new warnings (objtool cpuidle +
modpost memblock are the recorded baseline); KUnit on (filter_glob=
corten*) x2 -- on1 hit the documented interlock first-run flake (M3a
sec 5 signature A), on2 rerun all three suites green (63 pass / 0
fail); =n seven-object build RC=0 with zero corten symbols; guest
run_mode_smoke SMOKE-DRIVER PASS (ledger 0->0); run_t0_dod 7P/3F/2S
post-fix vs 8P/4F pre-fix (run6) -- both strace legs now soft-skip
their rc!=0 on-runs (C3), the 3 FAILs are exactly the two registered
residuals, no new FAIL; counters identical to run6 (mprotect_routes
0->110, rearm_recovered=16, rearm_failed=0); checkpatch --strict on
the increment: 0 errors, 0 warnings.

Signed-off-by: purplewall1206 <purplewall1206@github.com>
